<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 25 March, from 1306 to 1957.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1306">1306 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">720 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert the Bruce crowned King of Scots at Scone</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after killing his rival John Comyn, Bruce was crowned in defiance of Edward I. Defeated and hunted that year, he fought back to win at Bannockburn in 1314.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1655">1655 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">371 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christiaan Huygens discovers Titan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Using a telescope he had built with his brother, Huygens found Saturn's largest moon. Titan is now known to have a thick atmosphere and lakes of liquid methane.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain abolishes the slave trade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abolition-of-the-atlantic-slave-trade">Slave Trade Act</a> received royal assent, banning British participation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">Slavery</a> itself continued in British colonies until the Abolition Act of 1833.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1821">1821 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">205 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional start of the Greek War of Independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tradition holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Germanos of Patras raised the banner of revolt on this day. After years of war and great-power intervention, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> became independent in 1830.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1911">1911 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">115 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Triangle Shirtwaist Factory fire kills 146 in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire swept through a garment factory near Washington Square, and locked doors trapped workers, mostly young immigrant women. The disaster led to new fire safety and labour laws.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Rome signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and Luxembourg signed treaties creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a> and Euratom. The EEC grew into today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li></ol>
